  ('ai:ai-batch-06:df7a896dcb22','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to the text, why do many teenagers fall asleep late?',array['They are lazy.','They sleep during school lessons.','They use phones in bed.','Their bodies release melatonin later.']::text[],'D','''...the body releases the sleep hormone melatonin later in the evening.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Teenagers are often accused of being lazy when they stay in bed until midday at weekends. Yet sleep researchers argue that the problem is largely biological. During adolescence, the body releases the sleep hormone melatonin later in the evening, which means that many teenagers genuinely cannot fall asleep before eleven. Since school starts early, they build up a ''sleep debt'' during the week and try to repay it at weekends. Some schools in the UK and the US have experimented with later start times, reporting better attendance and concentration. Critics point out, however, that later starts create problems for parents'' working hours and for after-school activities.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:54d2aa44e9f8','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is a ''sleep debt''?',array['sleep lost during the week','sleep that costs money','sleeping too much at weekends','a sleeping problem in adults']::text[],'A','They ''build up a sleep debt during the week and try to repay it at weekends.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Teenagers are often accused of being lazy when they stay in bed until midday at weekends. Yet sleep researchers argue that the problem is largely biological. During adolescence, the body releases the sleep hormone melatonin later in the evening, which means that many teenagers genuinely cannot fall asleep before eleven. Since school starts early, they build up a ''sleep debt'' during the week and try to repay it at weekends. Some schools in the UK and the US have experimented with later start times, reporting better attendance and concentration. Critics point out, however, that later starts create problems for parents'' working hours and for after-school activities.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:43f7526120d9','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What did schools with later start times report?',array['more homework','fewer after-school clubs only','better attendance and concentration','worse exam results']::text[],'C','''...reporting better attendance and concentration.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Teenagers are often accused of being lazy when they stay in bed until midday at weekends. Yet sleep researchers argue that the problem is largely biological. During adolescence, the body releases the sleep hormone melatonin later in the evening, which means that many teenagers genuinely cannot fall asleep before eleven. Since school starts early, they build up a ''sleep debt'' during the week and try to repay it at weekends. Some schools in the UK and the US have experimented with later start times, reporting better attendance and concentration. Critics point out, however, that later starts create problems for parents'' working hours and for after-school activities.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:874b19925a39','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do critics say about later school starts?',array['They are too expensive.','They don''t help teenagers sleep.','Teachers don''t want them.','They cause problems for parents and activities.']::text[],'D','''Later starts create problems for parents'' working hours and for after-school activities.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Teenagers are often accused of being lazy when they stay in bed until midday at weekends. Yet sleep researchers argue that the problem is largely biological. During adolescence, the body releases the sleep hormone melatonin later in the evening, which means that many teenagers genuinely cannot fall asleep before eleven. Since school starts early, they build up a ''sleep debt'' during the week and try to repay it at weekends. Some schools in the UK and the US have experimented with later start times, reporting better attendance and concentration. Critics point out, however, that later starts create problems for parents'' working hours and for after-school activities.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:e2f28939f4f1','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the writer''s main point about teenagers sleeping late?',array['Schools should start at midday.','Parents should wake them earlier.','Teenagers should be punished.','It is mostly a biological issue, not laziness.']::text[],'D','''Sleep researchers argue that the problem is largely biological.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Teenagers are often accused of being lazy when they stay in bed until midday at weekends. Yet sleep researchers argue that the problem is largely biological. During adolescence, the body releases the sleep hormone melatonin later in the evening, which means that many teenagers genuinely cannot fall asleep before eleven. Since school starts early, they build up a ''sleep debt'' during the week and try to repay it at weekends. Some schools in the UK and the US have experimented with later start times, reporting better attendance and concentration. Critics point out, however, that later starts create problems for parents'' working hours and for after-school activities.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:1510b704f021','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to the text, what is NOT given as a cause of empty high-street shops?',array['bad weather','expensive parking','out-of-town shopping centres','online shopping']::text[],'A','The causes listed are online shopping, business rates, parking and out-of-town centres.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Across Britain, high streets that once thrived are now lined with empty shops. Online shopping is the most obvious cause, but it is not the only one: high business rates, expensive parking and the growth of out-of-town shopping centres have all played a part. Some towns are fighting back by reinventing their centres as places to spend time rather than simply to buy things. Empty units have been turned into community spaces, small workshops and cafés, and markets have been revived. The towns that succeed, experts say, are those that offer an experience that cannot be downloaded.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:f464f94f942f','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How are some towns reinventing their centres?',array['by closing markets','by making them places to spend time','by lowering online prices','by building more car parks']::text[],'B','''...reinventing their centres as places to spend time rather than simply to buy things.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Across Britain, high streets that once thrived are now lined with empty shops. Online shopping is the most obvious cause, but it is not the only one: high business rates, expensive parking and the growth of out-of-town shopping centres have all played a part. Some towns are fighting back by reinventing their centres as places to spend time rather than simply to buy things. Empty units have been turned into community spaces, small workshops and cafés, and markets have been revived. The towns that succeed, experts say, are those that offer an experience that cannot be downloaded.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:aacc2bbccfe8','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do successful towns offer, according to experts?',array['free parking','big chain stores','the cheapest prices','an experience you can''t get online']::text[],'D','''...an experience that cannot be downloaded.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Across Britain, high streets that once thrived are now lined with empty shops. Online shopping is the most obvious cause, but it is not the only one: high business rates, expensive parking and the growth of out-of-town shopping centres have all played a part. Some towns are fighting back by reinventing their centres as places to spend time rather than simply to buy things. Empty units have been turned into community spaces, small workshops and cafés, and markets have been revived. The towns that succeed, experts say, are those that offer an experience that cannot be downloaded.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:1724dfe1229b','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does ''thrived'' mean in the first sentence?',array['were very successful','were empty','were old-fashioned','were dangerous']::text[],'A','The high streets ''once thrived'' — they were busy and successful in the past.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Across Britain, high streets that once thrived are now lined with empty shops. Online shopping is the most obvious cause, but it is not the only one: high business rates, expensive parking and the growth of out-of-town shopping centres have all played a part. Some towns are fighting back by reinventing their centres as places to spend time rather than simply to buy things. Empty units have been turned into community spaces, small workshops and cafés, and markets have been revived. The towns that succeed, experts say, are those that offer an experience that cannot be downloaded.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:eceb9c1d03c2','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to the text, what happens when we remember an event?',array['We remember only the end.','We always forget details.','We replay an exact recording.','We rebuild it and may change it.']::text[],'D','''Each time we recall an event, we rebuild it.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Most of us believe that our memories work like video recordings, faithfully storing what happened. Psychological research suggests otherwise. Each time we recall an event, we rebuild it, and in doing so we can unknowingly add details or change them. In one well-known experiment, participants who watched a film of a car accident gave higher estimates of the cars'' speed when asked how fast they were going when they ''smashed'' into each other than when the word ''hit'' was used. A week later, those in the ''smashed'' group were also more likely to remember seeing broken glass, although there had been none.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:417f276178e8','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In the experiment, what did the word ''smashed'' affect?',array['the number of cars','people''s estimates of speed','the colour of the cars','the length of the film']::text[],'B','Participants gave higher estimates of speed when ''smashed'' was used.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Most of us believe that our memories work like video recordings, faithfully storing what happened. Psychological research suggests otherwise. Each time we recall an event, we rebuild it, and in doing so we can unknowingly add details or change them. In one well-known experiment, participants who watched a film of a car accident gave higher estimates of the cars'' speed when asked how fast they were going when they ''smashed'' into each other than when the word ''hit'' was used. A week later, those in the ''smashed'' group were also more likely to remember seeing broken glass, although there had been none.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:ca5046c16ae7','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What did the ''smashed'' group remember a week later?',array['a second accident','the cars'' colours','broken glass that wasn''t there','the drivers'' faces']::text[],'C','''More likely to remember seeing broken glass, although there had been none.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Most of us believe that our memories work like video recordings, faithfully storing what happened. Psychological research suggests otherwise. Each time we recall an event, we rebuild it, and in doing so we can unknowingly add details or change them. In one well-known experiment, participants who watched a film of a car accident gave higher estimates of the cars'' speed when asked how fast they were going when they ''smashed'' into each other than when the word ''hit'' was used. A week later, those in the ''smashed'' group were also more likely to remember seeing broken glass, although there had been none.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:401a81e7f08f','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the main idea of the text?',array['Memories can be changed without us knowing.','People lie about accidents.','Videos are better than memory.','Car accidents are hard to remember.']::text[],'A','The text argues memory is rebuilt and can unknowingly change.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Most of us believe that our memories work like video recordings, faithfully storing what happened. Psychological research suggests otherwise. Each time we recall an event, we rebuild it, and in doing so we can unknowingly add details or change them. In one well-known experiment, participants who watched a film of a car accident gave higher estimates of the cars'' speed when asked how fast they were going when they ''smashed'' into each other than when the word ''hit'' was used. A week later, those in the ''smashed'' group were also more likely to remember seeing broken glass, although there had been none.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:0e0cf49f3aa3','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does rewilding involve?',array['building tourist hotels','letting forests grow back and returning lost species','banning visitors','farming more sheep']::text[],'B','''...allow forests to regenerate and reintroduce species that disappeared long ago.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','In parts of Scotland, landowners are ''rewilding'' their estates: rather than managing the land for sheep or shooting, they allow forests to regenerate and reintroduce species that disappeared long ago. Supporters argue that rewilding increases biodiversity, stores carbon and can bring jobs through tourism. Opponents, many of them farmers, fear it threatens traditional ways of life and worry about the impact of predators on livestock. The debate is particularly heated over proposals to bring back the lynx, a wild cat that has been absent from Britain for over a thousand years.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:a898d76b1415','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which benefit of rewilding is mentioned?',array['storing carbon','cheaper food','better roads','more sheep farms']::text[],'A','''Rewilding increases biodiversity, stores carbon and can bring jobs.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','In parts of Scotland, landowners are ''rewilding'' their estates: rather than managing the land for sheep or shooting, they allow forests to regenerate and reintroduce species that disappeared long ago. Supporters argue that rewilding increases biodiversity, stores carbon and can bring jobs through tourism. Opponents, many of them farmers, fear it threatens traditional ways of life and worry about the impact of predators on livestock. The debate is particularly heated over proposals to bring back the lynx, a wild cat that has been absent from Britain for over a thousand years.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:4a461cdeb0f6','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why are farmers worried about the lynx?',array['It is too expensive.','It might attack their animals.','It eats trees.','It would bring too many tourists.']::text[],'B','''...worry about the impact of predators on livestock.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','In parts of Scotland, landowners are ''rewilding'' their estates: rather than managing the land for sheep or shooting, they allow forests to regenerate and reintroduce species that disappeared long ago. Supporters argue that rewilding increases biodiversity, stores carbon and can bring jobs through tourism. Opponents, many of them farmers, fear it threatens traditional ways of life and worry about the impact of predators on livestock. The debate is particularly heated over proposals to bring back the lynx, a wild cat that has been absent from Britain for over a thousand years.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:4df41a737029','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How long has the lynx been absent from Britain?',array['about a hundred years','over a thousand years','it has never lived there','since 2021']::text[],'B','''...absent from Britain for over a thousand years.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','In parts of Scotland, landowners are ''rewilding'' their estates: rather than managing the land for sheep or shooting, they allow forests to regenerate and reintroduce species that disappeared long ago. Supporters argue that rewilding increases biodiversity, stores carbon and can bring jobs through tourism. Opponents, many of them farmers, fear it threatens traditional ways of life and worry about the impact of predators on livestock. The debate is particularly heated over proposals to bring back the lynx, a wild cat that has been absent from Britain for over a thousand years.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:c602d6d21a96','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to critics, who benefits most from app-work flexibility?',array['the companies','the workers','customers only','the government']::text[],'A','''Critics argue that this flexibility mostly benefits the companies.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Freelance work arranged through apps — delivering food, driving taxis, doing small online tasks — is often praised for its flexibility. Workers can choose when to log on and can combine several jobs. But critics argue that this flexibility mostly benefits the companies. Because app workers are usually classed as self-employed, they are not entitled to holiday pay or sick pay, and their income can fall suddenly if the company changes how it pays. In 2021 the UK Supreme Court ruled that drivers for one large company should be treated as workers, with rights to the minimum wage and paid holidays.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:5b8707781bdc','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why don''t app workers usually get holiday pay?',array['They don''t ask for it.','They are classed as self-employed.','They work too few hours.','The law forbids it.']::text[],'B','''Because app workers are usually classed as self-employed, they are not entitled to holiday pay.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Freelance work arranged through apps — delivering food, driving taxis, doing small online tasks — is often praised for its flexibility. Workers can choose when to log on and can combine several jobs. But critics argue that this flexibility mostly benefits the companies. Because app workers are usually classed as self-employed, they are not entitled to holiday pay or sick pay, and their income can fall suddenly if the company changes how it pays. In 2021 the UK Supreme Court ruled that drivers for one large company should be treated as workers, with rights to the minimum wage and paid holidays.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:23d1a81fb8a3','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What did the Supreme Court decide in 2021?',array['All delivery riders are employees.','App work should be banned.','Some drivers should have workers'' rights.','Companies can set any pay.']::text[],'C','''Drivers for one large company should be treated as workers, with rights to the minimum wage and paid holidays.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Freelance work arranged through apps — delivering food, driving taxis, doing small online tasks — is often praised for its flexibility. Workers can choose when to log on and can combine several jobs. But critics argue that this flexibility mostly benefits the companies. Because app workers are usually classed as self-employed, they are not entitled to holiday pay or sick pay, and their income can fall suddenly if the company changes how it pays. In 2021 the UK Supreme Court ruled that drivers for one large company should be treated as workers, with rights to the minimum wage and paid holidays.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:91434f47416f','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What can happen to app workers'' income?',array['It is paid yearly.','It always rises.','It can fall suddenly.','It is fixed by law.']::text[],'C','''Their income can fall suddenly if the company changes how it pays.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Freelance work arranged through apps — delivering food, driving taxis, doing small online tasks — is often praised for its flexibility. Workers can choose when to log on and can combine several jobs. But critics argue that this flexibility mostly benefits the companies. Because app workers are usually classed as self-employed, they are not entitled to holiday pay or sick pay, and their income can fall suddenly if the company changes how it pays. In 2021 the UK Supreme Court ruled that drivers for one large company should be treated as workers, with rights to the minimum wage and paid holidays.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:c81c09f7b8b6','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What was the old belief about bilingual children?',array['They would be more intelligent.','They would be confused and fall behind.','They would learn faster.','They would forget their first language.']::text[],'B','''It was assumed that children who grow up speaking two languages would be confused and fall behind.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','For years it was assumed that children who grow up speaking two languages would be confused and fall behind at school. More recent research has largely overturned this view. Bilingual children may initially have a smaller vocabulary in each language, but their total vocabulary is usually similar to that of monolingual children. Some studies have also suggested that switching between languages trains the brain to ignore distractions, although this claimed ''bilingual advantage'' remains controversial, as several large studies have failed to find it.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:b1ed34f335e5','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does research say about bilingual children''s vocabulary?',array['It stops growing early.','It is always smaller.','The total is usually similar to monolingual children''s.','It is much larger in each language.']::text[],'C','''Their total vocabulary is usually similar to that of monolingual children.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','For years it was assumed that children who grow up speaking two languages would be confused and fall behind at school. More recent research has largely overturned this view. Bilingual children may initially have a smaller vocabulary in each language, but their total vocabulary is usually similar to that of monolingual children. Some studies have also suggested that switching between languages trains the brain to ignore distractions, although this claimed ''bilingual advantage'' remains controversial, as several large studies have failed to find it.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:d4962ad567fe','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why is the ''bilingual advantage'' controversial?',array['Several large studies did not find it.','Teachers disagree with it.','It only works for adults.','It makes children tired.']::text[],'A','''...several large studies have failed to find it.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','For years it was assumed that children who grow up speaking two languages would be confused and fall behind at school. More recent research has largely overturned this view. Bilingual children may initially have a smaller vocabulary in each language, but their total vocabulary is usually similar to that of monolingual children. Some studies have also suggested that switching between languages trains the brain to ignore distractions, although this claimed ''bilingual advantage'' remains controversial, as several large studies have failed to find it.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:96b5fcfb4b94','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does ''overturned'' mean in the text?',array['made stronger','turned upside down','forgotten','shown to be wrong']::text[],'D','Research has ''largely overturned this view'' — shown it to be largely wrong.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','For years it was assumed that children who grow up speaking two languages would be confused and fall behind at school. More recent research has largely overturned this view. Bilingual children may initially have a smaller vocabulary in each language, but their total vocabulary is usually similar to that of monolingual children. Some studies have also suggested that switching between languages trains the brain to ignore distractions, although this claimed ''bilingual advantage'' remains controversial, as several large studies have failed to find it.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:2aa589a55337','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why is the writer complaining about the delivery?',array['It was delivered to the wrong address.','It was cheaper than expected.','It arrived six days late despite paying for next-day delivery.','It arrived damaged.']::text[],'C','Ordered 3 May with next-day delivery, it came on 9 May.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Dear Customer Services, I am writing to complain about the washing machine I ordered from your website on 3 May. Although I paid extra for next-day delivery, it did not arrive until 9 May, and I had to take two days off work to wait for it. When it was finally installed, it leaked water across the kitchen floor during its first cycle. I would like you to collect the machine and either replace it or give me a full refund, including the delivery charge. I would also appreciate some compensation for the time I have lost. I look forward to hearing from you within seven days. Yours faithfully, R. Okafor',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:3d2e14c8b9a7','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What happened when the machine was first used?',array['It broke the kitchen door.','It was too noisy.','It didn''t switch on.','It leaked water.']::text[],'D','''It leaked water across the kitchen floor during its first cycle.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Dear Customer Services, I am writing to complain about the washing machine I ordered from your website on 3 May. Although I paid extra for next-day delivery, it did not arrive until 9 May, and I had to take two days off work to wait for it. When it was finally installed, it leaked water across the kitchen floor during its first cycle. I would like you to collect the machine and either replace it or give me a full refund, including the delivery charge. I would also appreciate some compensation for the time I have lost. I look forward to hearing from you within seven days. Yours faithfully, R. Okafor',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:4f6d792c2342','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which of these does the writer NOT ask for?',array['compensation for lost time','a replacement or full refund','a discount on a new machine','collection of the machine']::text[],'C','They ask for collection, replacement or refund including delivery, and compensation.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Dear Customer Services, I am writing to complain about the washing machine I ordered from your website on 3 May. Although I paid extra for next-day delivery, it did not arrive until 9 May, and I had to take two days off work to wait for it. When it was finally installed, it leaked water across the kitchen floor during its first cycle. I would like you to collect the machine and either replace it or give me a full refund, including the delivery charge. I would also appreciate some compensation for the time I have lost. I look forward to hearing from you within seven days. Yours faithfully, R. Okafor',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:38f11d93fb85','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the tone of the letter?',array['formal and firm','friendly and casual','angry and rude','humorous']::text[],'A','The letter is formal (''Yours faithfully'') and makes clear demands.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Dear Customer Services, I am writing to complain about the washing machine I ordered from your website on 3 May. Although I paid extra for next-day delivery, it did not arrive until 9 May, and I had to take two days off work to wait for it. When it was finally installed, it leaked water across the kitchen floor during its first cycle. I would like you to collect the machine and either replace it or give me a full refund, including the delivery charge. I would also appreciate some compensation for the time I have lost. I look forward to hearing from you within seven days. Yours faithfully, R. Okafor',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:da1b1ef1a392','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why did the writer lose two days of work?',array['to wait for the delivery','to visit the shop','to buy another machine','to clean the kitchen']::text[],'A','''I had to take two days off work to wait for it.''',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Dear Customer Services, I am writing to complain about the washing machine I ordered from your website on 3 May. Although I paid extra for next-day delivery, it did not arrive until 9 May, and I had to take two days off work to wait for it. When it was finally installed, it leaked water across the kitchen floor during its first cycle. I would like you to collect the machine and either replace it or give me a full refund, including the delivery charge. I would also appreciate some compensation for the time I have lost. I look forward to hearing from you within seven days. Yours faithfully, R. Okafor',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:87985031bd93','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What does the writer mean by ''an experience that cannot be downloaded''?',array['expensive shopping','free online films','something you can only enjoy in person','a website that does not work']::text[],'C','It means experiences you have to go to the town centre to enjoy.',array['exam','reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06','Across Britain, high streets that once thrived are now lined with empty shops. Online shopping is the most obvious cause, but it is not the only one: high business rates, expensive parking and the growth of out-of-town shopping centres have all played a part. Some towns are fighting back by reinventing their centres as places to spend time rather than simply to buy things. Empty units have been turned into community spaces, small workshops and cafés, and markets have been revived. The towns that succeed, experts say, are those that offer an experience that cannot be downloaded.',null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:c670d7d78111','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I''d sooner ___ than take the bus in this heat.',array['walked','walking','to walk','walk']::text[],'D','''Would sooner'' + base form, like ''would rather''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:8afb90e72f44','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','He was made ___ the form again.',array['filled in','filling in','to fill in','fill in']::text[],'C','In the passive, ''make'' is followed by ''to'' + verb.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:d9b8228ac916','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Should you need any help, ___ hesitate to ask.',array['not','didn''t','won''t','don''t']::text[],'D','''Should you...'' = ''If you...''; the main clause is an imperative.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:30cd0f416721','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','She left early ___ she would miss the traffic.',array['so as','so that','for','in order']::text[],'B','''So that'' + clause expresses purpose.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:9e379c8165a2','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The new hospital is ___ completed next year.',array['be','to be','to being','being']::text[],'B','''Be to be + past participle'' for planned future events.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:9026b2ec67ba','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','He talks as if he ___ everything.',array['has known','knows already','knew','would know']::text[],'C','''As if'' + past simple for an unreal present.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:e2f27f8ca174','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Many of the students, ___ were from abroad, found the course difficult.',array['the most of whom','most of them','most of whom','most who']::text[],'C','After a quantifier in a relative clause: ''most of whom''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:6c5531e57ccf','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I can''t help ___ that something is wrong.',array['feel','felt','to feel','feeling']::text[],'D','''Can''t help + -ing''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:3c6644751704','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The interview went well; the panel seemed ___ by her ideas.',array['impressed','impression','impressing','impressive']::text[],'A','People are impressed by something impressive.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:501b10ac944d','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','We had to ___ a compromise between cost and quality.',array['hit','push','beat','strike']::text[],'D','''Strike a compromise / balance''.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:bcb753ae30f8','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The firm has been ___ losses for three years.',array['having made of','doing','taking','making']::text[],'D','Businesses make a profit or a loss.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:1d9be567a482','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','He has a ___ for exaggerating his achievements.',array['tension','tenderness','tendency','tenancy']::text[],'C','A tendency is a habit of behaving in a certain way.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:efd046ee646d','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The city ___ a population of over two million.',array['has','contains of','keeps','holds of']::text[],'A','A city has a population of...',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:7b23f10bd168','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','I''d like to ___ my thanks to everyone who helped.',array['express','impress','suppress','press']::text[],'A','To express thanks is to say them.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:cd2b40e56b29','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The view from the top was absolutely ___.',array['breathless','breathtaking','breathing','breath-taken']::text[],'B','Breathtaking means extremely beautiful.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:7491a951c05b','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Their marriage ___ after only two years.',array['broke down into','broke up','broke in','broke out']::text[],'B','''Break up'' means end a relationship.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:ab0c9dbfb217','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','A war ___ out in 1914.',array['broken','burst','broke up','broke']::text[],'D','''War broke out'' means it started.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:75c18010a091','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The team ___ a narrow defeat in the final.',array['sustained to','supported','suffocated','suffered']::text[],'D','You suffer a defeat.',array['exam','vocabulary']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:0d4f0802db6d','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Not once ___ to apologise for the mistake.',array['offered he','he did offer','did he offer','he offered']::text[],'C','Negative adverbials at the front trigger inversion: ''Not once did he...''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:7ba5cc2324a1','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','___ it not been for the rain, the match would have been finished.',array['Were','Should','Had','If']::text[],'C','''Had it not been for'' = ''If it had not been for''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:12d87e220ec4','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The proposal, ___ merits are undeniable, was nonetheless rejected.',array['which','of which its','its','whose']::text[],'D','''Whose'' can refer to things: the proposal''s merits.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:90c5a5b5bcad','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','She is reputed ___ a fortune in the 1990s.',array['to make','to have made','having made','that she made']::text[],'B','Reporting verbs + perfect infinitive for past events.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:6955da4ed850','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','So ___ was the storm that all flights were grounded.',array['severely','severe','severity','a severe']::text[],'B','''So + adjective + be + subject'' (inversion) for emphasis.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:e9bea2490609','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','It is essential that every applicant ___ a valid passport.',array['will have','have','has','had']::text[],'B','The subjunctive uses the base form after ''essential that''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-06:8f9c6600e64a','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I''d have helped you, ___ you asked.',array['if','had','were','should']::text[],'B','Inverted conditional: ''had you asked'' = ''if you had asked''.',array['exam','grammar']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-06',null,null,null,null,'exam'),
